# Overrides. You do not need any of these.
#
# The app already points at the live dSCRT deployment, so a fresh clone builds and runs
# against it with no configuration at all. Copy this file only if you are pointing a fork
# somewhere else — a devnet, or mainnet when there is one.
#
# Everything here is public: the app is a static export with no server, so nothing in it is
# a secret. All of it is compiled into the bundle at build time, so changing one means
# rebuilding. An empty value is treated the same as an absent one.

# NEXT_PUBLIC_CHAIN_ID=pulsar-3
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LCD_URL=https://pulsar.lcd.secretnodes.com
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CORE_ADDRESS=secret1lj23n74aan7nlgj6hfm45fh3gc7h2ctdplsw8y
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TOKEN_ADDRESS=secret1hvt29j32a9k839n057p9qr75mgake8y9yjurq3

# Pin the code hashes rather than asking the chain for them.
#
# Leave these out and the app resolves them at runtime, which is what lets it follow a
# contract migration without a redeploy. Set them and it uses yours and never looks: a
# deliberate refusal to follow the contract admin anywhere, at the cost of every query
# dying the moment they migrate.
#
# Setting these in a hosting dashboard "to be safe" is the single most likely way to break
# a working deployment. They are not safety. They are a pin.

# NEXT_PUBLIC_CORE_CODE_HASH=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TOKEN_CODE_HASH=
